{"actor":"agent:qa-userflow","data":{"description":"Step-6 cross-machine flow: cloned the bare remote; the clone has 0 etch refs by default (git doesn't fetch custom ref namespaces). An explicit 'git fetch origin refs/etch/sessions/*:refs/etch/sessions/*' brings them over and they parse fine, and 'query' works in the clone. But a naive user on machine 2 who just 'git pull's will see NO etch data and not know why. README should add a one-liner: after cloning, run 'entire-agent-etch setup-refspec' (or the explicit fetch refspec) in the clone so 'git fetch' pulls session refs.","priority":"low","short_id":"ETCH-24","status":"backlog","title":"Fresh clone does not auto-fetch etch refs until setup-refspec is rerun in the clone \u2014 undocumented","type":"bug"},"id":"ev_01KSTXJG8SW8S08C6GYD2WWS7D","schema_version":1,"task_id":"task_01KSTXJG8Q2ZWH849E12QJKHCV","ts":"2026-05-29T22:27:12Z","type":"task_created"}
